<title>USA: Horry County, S.C., okays baseball stadium plan.</title>
<headline>Horry County, S.C., okays baseball stadium plan.</headline>
<dateline>CONWAY, S.C. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Carolina's Horry County Council has approved plans to build an $11 million minor-league baseball stadium, The State reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The proposal was approved in a 6-5 vote. The City of Myrtle Beach has agreed to pay 70 percent of the costs and the county will pay 30 percent. Construction will begin immediately</p>
<p>The facility will house the Durham Bulls, a Clas A farm team for the Atlanta Braves. The team is moving to South Carolina from Durham, N.C.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
</text>
